{
  "about": "Frankendom parts, stage 2 fit rows (Dom 2026-10-28: 'you become what you kill'). One row per body that can wear or donate a part: `id` is the data/profiles.json id (or `hero` for the player's body, which is no profile), `measuredOn` is the OpenTrident parts-manifest body id the numbers were measured on (MIT, tools/parts-lab/parts_manifest.mjs; mapped by name; the Minotaur body is profile `pitborn`, ch25-nonpbr). A donor row also carries OpenTrident's boss-cuts review (PR #11, 2026-10-30; the hero row has none of these): `wearable` (the Equip button is offered only for a wearable donor; false until its art is fixed), `quality` (1 = best, unique), `source` (`derived` = load OpenTrident's site/models/boss-cuts-derived/<stem>-106.cut.derived.glb, `original` = V3's own src/assets file) and `reason`. The hero row is the body the part is worn on, named by `hero` (it is no profile). `measure`: metres from the body's 106-joint bind pose (height, thigh and shin length for the leg lift, shoulder width and limb radii for the collars); `null` = no measure row, so the lift is 0 and there are no collars (OpenTrident's rule; Kachujin has none). `collars`: the five seam rings (src/fight/parts-fit.ts collarRows builds them from `measure` by the rules in data/parts.json `fit.collar`; a test pins that the stored rows equal what the rules give): bone, `at` = fraction of the bone's length to its first child, radius `r` and height `h` in metres. Values are checked by src/parts-fit-rows.ts validateFitRows at load; keys by src/sim/validate.js. Known odd rows, kept as OpenTrident measured them: the-boss (height_m 0.538 and no thigh_r: the hip rings are too small) and castle-guard (OpenTrident has two bodies, castle-guard-01 and -02; 01 taken, heights differ by 0.06 m).",
